        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terra_Ceia%2C_Florida",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1539, Hernando De Soto and his men camped at Terra Ceia’s mounds for six weeks before continuing south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terra_Ceia%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Citrus cultivation exploded after the 1880s, and early‑1900s railroads brought packing houses that amplified the island’s agricultural output.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
